{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":""More News from Nowhere" is the 28th single by Australian rock band Nick Cave and the Bad Seeds and the second single from the album "Dig, Lazarus, Dig!!!","title":"More News from Nowhere"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":"".","title":"More News from Nowhere"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The song has a melodic similarity to "Deanna" from the 1988 album "Tender Prey" and the song also mentions the character of Deanna.","title":"More News from Nowhere"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The title is a reference to novel "News From Nowhere" by William Morris.","title":"More News from Nowhere"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" It also includes many elements taken from the Odyssey.","title":"More News from Nowhere"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" The video was directed by British artists Iain Forsyth and Jane Pollard, who also directed videos for the other singles from this album.","title":"More News from Nowhere"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" It was filmed at the Raymond Revuebar and featured cameo appearances from author Will Self, actors Michael Higgs, Caroline Catz and Karl Theobald, socialite Peaches Geldof, singer/songwriter Beth Orton, British artists Tim Noble and Sue Webster and bass player for The Wonder Stuff Mark McCarthy along with a number of burlesque dancers.","title":"More News from Nowhere"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" The video was cut to the full-length album version of the song, running to over seven minutes.","title":"More News from Nowhere"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":""I Want You So Hard (Boy's Bad News)" is the first single from the Eagles of Death Metal's second studio album "Death By Sexy".","title":"I Want You So Hard (Boy's Bad News)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The song and music video has Jack Black, Josh Homme and Dave Grohl (all in wigs) making guest appearances.","title":"I Want You So Hard (Boy's Bad News)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The video was directed by Akiva Schaffer, who directs the SNL Digital Shorts on "Saturday Night Live", in